   "subject": "New shiny package - easyslider",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I started working on a package to make basic shiny UIs a bit more straightforward. The main idea is to map UI components to variables in the dataset, like ggplot2 does for plots.<div><br></div><div>For example:<br><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-family:SFMono-Regular,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:13.6px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:1.45;word-wrap:normal;padding:16px;overflow:auto;background-color:rgb(246,248,250);border-radius:3px;word-break:normal;color:rgb(36,41,46)\">   <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">df</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">&lt;-</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">diamonds</span> %<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">&gt;</span>%\r\n     slider2Filter(aes(<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">depth</span>)) %<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">&gt;</span>%\r\n     dropdownFilter(aes(<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">clarity</span>))\r\n\r\n   <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">output</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">$</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">distPlot</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">&lt;-</span> renderPlot({\r\n       df() %<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">&gt;</span>% ggplot() <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">+</span> aes(<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(227,98,9)\">x</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">=</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">carat</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(227,98,9)\">y</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">=</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">price</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(227,98,9)\">color</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">=</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">cut</span>) <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">+</span> geom_point()\r\n     })\r\n</pre></div><div><br></div><div>I just wanted to see if there is broader interest in this approach.</div><div><br></div><div>Source code here: <a href=\"https://github.com/nfultz/easyslider\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/nfultz/easyslider&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792389526897000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3OqFc5fTFqvdi7qaSF26xX\">https://github.com/nfultz/easyslider</a><br></div></div><div><br></div><div>-Neal</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
